The indigenous population has remained absolutely unchanged, and they are still just as in need of adaptation.
Over time, as the population began to adapt to its new environment, it became less and less similar to the other population.
Eventually, after thousands or even millions of years, the two populations look so different that they cannot be considered members of a single species.
