Proteins found in legumes and cereals would be the easiest plant-based sources to cultivate, but for primates like us, digesting them before cooking is difficult.
On the contrary, living organisms (crumbs, termites, eggs) are not only easily digestible but also provide high levels of protein containing all essential amino acids.
Given that everything has been taken into account, if our ancestors had solved their "protein problems" in a way similar to how modern savanna chimpanzees do, we shouldn't be surprised.
