For example, students at Bennet High School in North Carolina create a website each year about their trips to the state capital, the website is redesigned every year, but older versions are stored online to serve as albums.
Blogs also help improve students' writing skills. Although students often begin their blogging experience with basic grammar and spelling mistakes, the awareness of the classroom presence usually changes this.
Since students are often the most critical listeners, the blogger strives to improve what they write in order to avoid criticism.
At the same time, blogging encourages students to become more knowledgeable about the world around them. The need to satisfy public interest motivates students to become both knowledgeable and interesting (Toto, 2004).
Blogging is an inspiring tool for collaboration and encourages students to expand their knowledge beyond traditional classroom learning.
