The Oyapok River bridge is a suspension bridge. It stretches along the Oyapock River, connecting the city of Oiapoque in Brazil with the city of Saint-Georges-de-l'Oyapock in French Guiana.
The height of the two minarets reaches 83 meters, and they have two sidewalks, each 378 meters long and 3.5 meters wide.
